cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "A Priori Power Analysis Wizard"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Atzori"
    given-names: "Federico"
    affiliation: "University of Cagliari"
version: 1.4.2
date-released: 2026-08-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/federicoatz/apriori-power-wizard"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21804595
# The second identifier below pins the archived DOI for THIS file's own
# `version:` field above -- Zenodo assigns it automatically a few minutes
# after a GitHub release, so it can only be filled in as a follow-up edit,
# not in the release commit itself. It has gone stale (pointing at an
# earlier version than the one this file declares) three times already;
# check it whenever `version:` changes, and update paper.tex's matching
# Zenodo citations in the same pass.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21804595
    description: "Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest archived release"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21834275
    description: "Archived snapshot of version 1.2.3 on Zenodo -- STALE: this file now declares 1.4.2, whose DOI Zenodo has not minted yet. Replace both value and description once the 1.4.2 release is archived."
abstract: >-
  A step-by-step Shiny application that guides researchers in experimental
  economics and behavioral science through an a priori (before data
  collection) power analysis to determine required sample size, without
  assuming prior power-analysis experience.
keywords:
  - power analysis
  - sample size
  - experimental economics
  - behavioral science
  - R Shiny
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      A Priori Power Analysis Wizard: A Guided Interface for Choosing and
      Justifying Sample-Size Calculations in Behavioral Science
    authors:
      - family-names: "Atzori"
        given-names: "Federico"
        affiliation: "University of Cagliari"
    url: "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=7237018"
    notes: >-
      Working paper describing the design and validation of this software;
      posted to SSRN 2026-08-05, not yet peer-reviewed.
